  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1968-p26.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "We have \\(S=N(N+1).\\) For \\(N=999,\\) this is \\(999{,}000\\lt1{,}000{,}000,\\) while for \\(N=1000\\) it is \\(1{,}001{,}000.\\) Thus \\(N=1000,\\) whose digit sum is \\(1.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "The sum is \\(N(N+1)\\)",
        "Compare \\(999\\cdot1000\\) and \\(1000\\cdot1001\\) with one million"
